  "goodToKnow": "Der Kreuzzug is a crusade. The medieval Kreuzzüge (1096 onwards) also involved German rulers: Emperor Frederick Barbarossa drowned in 1190 in the Saleph river in Anatolia on the Third Crusade. The Crusades also brought massacres of Jewish communities in Rhineland cities like Mainz and Worms in 1096. Figuratively, einen Kreuzzug führen gegen means to campaign zealously. Plural: die Kreuzzüge."
